---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';

const path = '/use-cases/vip-segments';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/vip-segments');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/vip-segments');
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Design Shopify VIP customer campaigns</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">Recognize valuable customer relationships with benefits the store can reliably deliver, using a qualification policy customers and staff can understand.</p>
    <article class="prose-shopify card mt-12 max-w-4xl p-8">
      <h2>Define value and qualification</h2>
      <p>Choose whether eligibility follows net spend, repeat orders, tenure or another stated business goal. Gross spend can conceal returns and service costs. Specify the measurement window and how gifts, household identities and wholesale accounts are treated. Avoid labeling discount users as inherently less deserving.</p>
      <h2>Separate status from service recovery</h2>
      <p>Set a review and downgrade policy before inviting members, including treatment of late refunds. A customer complaint calls for resolution; silently removing status can conflict with an existing promise. Keep manual exceptions attributable to an owner with a reason and review date.</p>
      <h2>Choose benefits with capacity</h2>
      <p>Early access needs a real access path; personal service needs available staff; free shipping has a cost and destination limits. Explain benefit availability and avoid guaranteeing scarce inventory without a reservation mechanism. Compare the expected cost with contribution, not only the appeal of a larger discount.</p>
      <h2>Coordinate recognition across campaigns</h2>
      <p>Carry qualification to launch and loyalty workflows without enrolling a VIP in every available message. Keep earned loyalty rewards distinct from discretionary VIP recognition. A cart reminder should reflect a benefit already granted rather than manufacture another code that conflicts with it.</p>
      <h2>Proposed policy exercise</h2>
      <p>Qualify a staff profile, issue a benefit, then process a return that changes eligibility. Check the access mechanism and customer-facing explanation against the written policy. Compare retention and contribution including benefit costs and customers who never redeem; these are proposed checks, not evidence of a supplier’s capabilities.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
